  "summary_en": "UK government command paper establishing the AI Safety Institute, the first state-backed body focused on advanced AI safety. It sets out the mission, three functions (evaluations, foundational research, information exchange), partnerships, funding and definitions. The Institute is not a regulator and focuses on frontier AI, not robotics.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "AISI evolves from the Frontier AI Taskforce as a permanent state-backed body",
   "Three functions: system evaluations, foundational safety research, information exchange",
   "Evaluation priorities: dual-use capabilities, societal impacts, system safety/security, loss of control",
   "Not a regulator; evaluations do not designate systems safe or decide releases",
   "Funding continued annually from 2024-25 after initial £100m; hosts secretariat for State of the Science Report"
